WEBVTT

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.940
Okay, all done.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:12.370
I finished the substitute
Noela, full body edition.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.060
Oh, it looks just like Ms. Noela!

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:21.650
Exactly. I thought our part-timer
could make do with this.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.050
Expecting Noela to put up with him
every time he's here would be rough.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.600
Wel...come...

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.200
Hey, it's the Valgas's butler, uh...

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.010
It's Rayne. Pardon me.

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:38.700
Can we help you with something today?

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.430
Yes. Mr. Reiji, my master
would like to see you.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.140
Your master?

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.080
You mean Elaine's father?

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.350
Woof?

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:24.450
Thank you for helping my wife the other day.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:29.120
Because of you, everyone at the
dinner party was talking about her.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.980
Elaine was able to get some work
experience at your store... as well.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.960
I'm truly grateful to you.

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:40.430
Uh, sure... So, what can I do for you today?

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.100
About that...

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:48.850
Recently, my daughter Elaine
has begun avoiding me.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.190
Avoiding you?

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:51.230
Don't play dumb!

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:51.880
Huh?

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.680
I know what you're up to!

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:54.110
What?!

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:58.880
If you want my daughter,
you'll have to defeat me first!

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:00.200
Why would I need to do that?!

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:04.620
How dare you use such underhanded
psychological attacks against me,

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.020
your most difficult opponent?!

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:07.800
It's not like that!

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:13.540
Ms. Elaine's behavior is most
likely caused by puberty.

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:16.250
Puberty?

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:19.440
I've heard that girls going through puberty

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:25.370
tend to develop a temporary dislike
of their fathers based on their gender.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:29.510
But my daughter used to adore me!

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:33.320
Daddy, I love you!

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:38.170
I'm gonna marry you someday, Daddy!

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.780
Are you, now?

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.940
She used to say that to me!

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:44.240
Even so!

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:47.450
Adolescent girls from every
world go through a period

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:51.710
when they don't want to mix up
their laundry with their father's.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.880
Laundry? Come to think
of it, the other day...

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.770
Elaine, I'm coming in.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:02.840
Okay. What is it, Father?

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:06.800
This was mixed in with my laundry.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:19.370
H-Huh?

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:23.050
Elaine looked at me as though I were garbage.

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.280
Yeah, I'm sure she did.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:28.640
But Elaine is still too young
for that type of underwear.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:29.320
Huh?

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:30.860
Who does she intend to show it off to?

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:31.910
Dunno...

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:33.280
It's disgraceful, truly disgraceful.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.150
Did you tell her that?

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:35.740
Of course!

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:38.100
That's the worst thing you could've done!

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.880
What? Really?

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:43.800
She'll think you see her as
more than just your daughter.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.230
But I'm just worried about her.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:48.390
Even so!

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.040
Her father is her father.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:54.020
She doesn't want to see an ounce
of the opposite sex in him.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:57.530
Does this mean my daughter hates me now?

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.110
Mr. Reiji.

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:01.080
Oh, Elaine.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:05.640
I heard from our butler that you were here.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:10.500
What did you invite
Mr. Reiji here to discuss?

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:12.910
Well, uh...

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:15.930
I think I have an idea.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:19.140
Mr. Reiji, rather than spending
time with my dirty father...

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:20.520
D-Dirty?!

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.790
Let's go to my room where we
can have a nice chat together.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.390
But—

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.910
Hurry, this way.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.870
Elaine, wait!

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:32.270
Elaine...

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:37.480
You know, you didn't have to put it that way.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.680
Your dad's probably crying right now.

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:41.980
Yes, but...

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:47.400
Your dad has his faults, but it's
not as if you hate him, right?

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.880
Well, of course.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:51.990
Then let's go apologize to him later, okay?

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:59.880
Elaine seems to be aware that
she spoke harshly to her father.

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:04.070
I wish there was something
I could do to get them to reconcile.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.800
Kirio Drugstore

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:10.230
Master! The botanical deodorant!

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:11.690
Thanks, Noela.

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:12.930
Woof.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:17.260
Mr. Reiji, what are you going to
do with that botanical deodorant?

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:19.760
I was wondering if I could tweak it a little.

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:25.190
By the way, why are you carrying
around the substitute Noela?

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:29.320
I tried applying some charm fragrance
to it so that it would smell nice.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:33.960
I'm sure Mr. Ejil would've preferred
for it to smell like Ms. Noela, though.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:37.170
You think he'd prefer Noela's smell?

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.790
I see! That's it!

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.120
I can do that!

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:03.840
It's done!

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:06.820
Sir,

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:11.610
using this medicine may resolve
your problem with Ms. Elaine.

00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:16.560
Odorless Body Soap.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:20.750
Removes the smell of sweat and
other odors. Also disinfects.

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:27.120
I see. You're saying that if I just
use this, Elaine will love me again?

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.770
I wouldn't go that far.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:33.180
What do you think?

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:35.470
Smells nice, doesn't it?

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:39.390
It's a good, simple smell.

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:43.060
Take my word for it and give it a try.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:46.520
I hate blindly trusting people.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.480
Then what will you do?

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:52.070
At this rate, your relationship
will continue to get worse.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:56.440
Your daughter may never make eye contact
with you again, much less speak to—

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:57.940
I'll definitely use this!

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:00.790
Someone prepare a bath!

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:04.000
Bathing In Progress

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:06.960
Huh? That's odd.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:09.060
He turned handsome?!

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:11.340
Your medicine is perfect.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:14.590
Well? What do you think of this
rejuvenated version of me?

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:17.440
His voice, tone, and
personality have changed, too!

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:20.790
Perhaps Elaine won't dislike me now.

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:22.810
Uh, I don't know about that.

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:27.240
I have a feeling Elaine will hate this, too.

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:31.050
Father, what do you—

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:32.470
Elaine!

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:34.360
Who is this man?!

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.450
Hey!

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.650
What are you doing?!

00:08:38.650 --> 00:08:41.270
Alchemist, why are you stopping me?

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:44.160
Of course I'm stopping you!
You can't just suddenly hug her!

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:47.930
You scared Ms. Elaine! Are you okay?

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:49.000
Mr. Reiji...

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.800
Get away from my daughter, alchemist!

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:55.950
Daughter? Wait, is that you, Father?

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:59.050
That's right, Elaine. It is I!

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:00.970
Why is he speaking like that
and striking that pose?

00:09:01.380 --> 00:09:04.290
Do I have to play along here?

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:06.810
Might as well.

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:12.900
Your daughter is mine, Casty!

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:15.880
Bastard, you've revealed your true colors!

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:18.900
You just now noticed?

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:24.560
By ensnaring your daughter and
marrying her, I'll become nobility.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.040
Marry?

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:29.210
Which means we'll be husband
and wife? I'm delighted!

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:32.490
Hey, I'm the bad guy here!
Don't make goo-goo eyes at me!

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:34.720
What are you doing?!

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:38.930
You deserve to die for
toying with my daughter!

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:43.210
I won't allow you to hurt Mr. Reiji.

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:46.960
Don't side with me! You're ruining the plan!

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:48.940
Everything is going according to my plan.

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:53.410
If my father won't approve of us,
then we'll have to elope!

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:55.240
Please shut up!

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:56.530
Hey, Casty!

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.490
Your daughter hates you, right?

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:03.400
She called you a smelly, creepy old pervert.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:04.940
She didn't say all that!

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:05.950
He's right.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:11.290
Wouldn't you prefer if your daughter
were gone? I'll take her instead.

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:16.340
I've never wished Elaine was gone!

00:10:17.310 --> 00:10:18.300
Father...

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:22.450
I've loved her since the moment
she was born! She's my child!

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:26.430
That doesn't mean it didn't hurt
when she began avoiding me.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:29.230
But so what?!

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:34.630
I trust that Elaine's dislike
for me is temporary.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:39.720
No matter what, I will
always be on Elaine's side.

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:44.710
I love you, Elaine.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:50.950
Father!

00:10:54.910 --> 00:10:59.300
I'm sorry. I was so cruel to you, Father.

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:12.650
Father, this pleasant smell...

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:16.710
This is the same perfume I use.

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:18.890
Mr. Reiji... Huh?

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:23.440
Mr. Reiji?

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:27.930
Two days later, I received
a letter from the lord,

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:32.830
thanking me and telling me that
I couldn't have his daughter.

00:11:34.140 --> 00:11:36.040
I replied that I was acting the other day

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:41.640
and not to worry because I had no intention
of taking his daughter from him.

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:52.960
I wish he hadn't been acting.

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:02.220
Mr. Reiji?

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:04.870
Sorry, did I wake you?

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:07.670
I made lunch. Can you eat?

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:09.860
Yes.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:16.530
Anyway, you don't often get fevers.
After all, you're a ghost.

00:12:16.530 --> 00:12:17.740
I know.

00:12:17.740 --> 00:12:20.270
I'll leave your lunch here, okay?

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:24.090
C-Could you feed it to me, please?

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:26.430
What? You don't think you can feed yourself?

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:34.210
It's not that. It's just that times like
these make me want to be spoiled, so...

00:12:40.430 --> 00:12:43.750
How is it? I'm not too
confident in my cooking.

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:47.750
It's good. It's seasoned just right.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:49.030
Oh, good.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:51.350
Here.

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:56.920
What is it?

00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:02.880
This was my room a long time ago.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:03.860
What?

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:08.350
I stared at this ceiling for so
long that I got sick of seeing it.

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:10.850
It hasn't changed at all.

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:16.270
Come to think of it, Mina mentioned
being sickly while she was alive.

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:20.480
My mother always took care
of me when I was sick.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:23.520
I caused so much trouble for her.

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:29.550
Ultimately, I died first from an illness.

00:13:36.610 --> 00:13:40.130
It's okay. Nobody thinks
you're causing trouble.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.040
I was a nuisance.

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:47.020
I made my entire family unhappy.

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:50.350
You should rest for now.

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:55.030
What? The boss isn't here? Too bad.

00:13:55.030 --> 00:13:58.230
How dare you take that attitude toward me?!

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:01.400
Do you know you're speaking
to Garo Ejil the Demon King?

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:03.190
What's that? Is it a tasty food?

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:04.450
What?!

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:06.420
Micott.

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:07.420
Woof.

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:09.490
Thanks, Noela. See you later.

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:11.290
Say "hi" to the boss for me.

00:14:11.290 --> 00:14:12.210
Woof.

00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:15.260
Hmph, what a bunch of rude customers.

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:19.210
Master.

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:21.540
Master, how's Mina?

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:23.220
She's sleeping soundly right now.

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:24.350
Will she get better?

00:14:24.350 --> 00:14:29.060
Her cold will, but she has
a more fundamental problem.

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:29.960
Woof?

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:35.220
Ejil, I want you to gather
the ingredients listed here.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:39.360
If you do, you can pet Noela's tail.

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:41.730
Not the substitute Noela, either.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:43.240
The real one.

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:46.090
The r-real... fluff...

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:50.140
I'm going to pet Ms. Noela!

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:50.900
Woof?

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:53.870
All right. Noela, could you
help me with something?

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:54.920
Woof.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:01.960
Hup. Down here, Noela.

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:02.730
Woof.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:08.420
Mina's family lived in this
house a hundred years ago.

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:14.480
And this was Mina's mother's room.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:16.870
I'm sure we'll find something useful in here.

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:20.880
What's this?

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:21.980
Woof?

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:24.230
The writing has faded.

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:28.070
Yeah, but some of it is legible.

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:32.440
It was Mina's mother's journal.

00:15:32.810 --> 00:15:36.980
Master! I got everything!

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:37.390
Woof. He's back.

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:40.340
That was quick! Such is the
power of ulterior motives.

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:43.050
Okay, it's all here.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.990
Thanks for the help, Ejil.

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:46.920
You're welcome.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:50.050
Anyway, our promise...

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:53.630
Oh, right. I'm not sure Noela
will allow it, though.

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:57.060
My tail? No way.

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:57.890
Huh?

00:15:57.890 --> 00:15:58.820
Woof!

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:10.380
It's done!

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.470
Three-Minute Revive.

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:16.750
Three-Minute Revive?

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:20.870
Yeah. By sprinkling a few drops
of that medicine on this,

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:24.830
we can bring your mother back
for just three minutes. Here.

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:25.880
What's this?

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:28.840
I'm pretty sure it's your mother's journal.

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:37.760
This is definitely my mother's handwriting.

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:40.720
But most of it is illegible.

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:44.200
It's up to you if you want
to use the medicine or not.

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.110
I'll use it.

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:50.320
Are you sure?

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:54.950
Yes. I want to know what my mother thought.

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:57.360
It's been a hundred years since then,

00:16:57.690 --> 00:17:02.790
but I believe I must accept it,
no matter how she felt.

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:07.940
Got it. Like I said, sprinkle
that medicine on the journal.

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:10.800
I'll be in the other room.

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:17.140
Mr. Reiji, could you...

00:17:17.610 --> 00:17:19.610
Could you hold my hand?

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:23.730
Okay, got it.

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:50.210
Why?

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:53.930
I thought she was cured, but she's
sick with something else now.

00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:57.470
We don't have any money left to buy medicine.

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:00.390
I'm sorry.

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:03.900
My husband leaves taking care
of our daughter entirely to me.

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:06.350
Why do I have to do everything?

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:13.970
She's right. I was stuck in bed
while my mother was by my side.

00:18:14.410 --> 00:18:16.630
Taking care of me must've been difficult.

00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:18.820
I'm really sorry.

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:20.370
Why?

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:22.960
Why won't she get better?

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:24.460
Don't ask me!

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:26.410
I wasn't sick because I wanted to be!

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.520
Why don't the medicines work?

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:29.660
I don't know!

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:32.500
The doctor said he doesn't know, either.

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:35.380
I don't know what to do anymore.

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:39.340
That's why I died first!

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:42.010
Isn't that what you preferred, Mother?

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:46.060
I couldn't bother anyone once I was dead!

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:52.020
Why, Mina? Why did you have to die before me?

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:58.190
You should have so much
happiness waiting for you,

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:02.410
but ultimately, I couldn't make you happy.

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:03.580
Huh?

00:19:03.970 --> 00:19:09.040
This was harder on you than
anyone else, wasn't it, Mina?

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:12.000
Mother...

00:19:12.870 --> 00:19:17.110
I think I was happy because I had you, Mina.

00:19:17.110 --> 00:19:18.610
Liar.

00:19:18.610 --> 00:19:24.180
After all, now that you're
gone, I miss you so much.

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:33.160
If you had found a boyfriend and married
him, I was going to give you that brooch.

00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:34.950
The brooch?

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:41.970
My mother gave it to me when I got married.

00:19:42.710 --> 00:19:45.300
Apparently my grandmother gave it to her.

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:51.890
That's when my mother told me
the meaning of that brooch.

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:53.170
Its meaning?

00:19:54.680 --> 00:19:56.470
"I hope you find happiness."

00:20:12.200 --> 00:20:14.720
Mother... Mother...

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:21.020
Mr. Reiji, thank you.

00:20:21.710 --> 00:20:22.620
It's okay.

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:26.170
I'm glad you got to see your mom.

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:28.440
Me, too.

00:20:30.570 --> 00:20:35.980
Mother, I am happy.

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:41.550
When I first met Mina in this house
that had been empty for years...

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:49.430
A g-ghost?!

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:55.140
I'm not a ghost. I used to
live here a hundred years ago.

00:20:55.140 --> 00:20:57.940
Th-That's what you call a ghost!

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:04.280
I'm not a ghost. I watch over the residents
of this house from the ceiling.

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:08.020
I'm what you'd call the
guardian spirit of the house.

00:21:08.020 --> 00:21:09.950
Guardian spirit?

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:14.290
But for some reason, everyone runs away
when they make eye contact with me.

00:21:14.290 --> 00:21:15.310
I bet they do.

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:18.250
I just have one wish:

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:23.450
for everyone who lives
here to have a happy life.

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:25.470
A happy life?

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:30.600
Yes. That alone is enough to satisfy me.

00:21:34.220 --> 00:21:41.160
Mina's mother, your feelings
reached your daughter.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:46.070
Closing Time

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:53.410
Thank you. See you later.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.250
Illustration by: Nanohanakohina
